y:\nTo ease the heavy energies of Saturn and Ketu, offer yellow sweets to the needy and chant the Guru mantra \'Om Brihaspataye Namah\' daily.','#B8860B','7','11:45 AM - 12:32 PM','⚖️ Balanced','Jupiter','Fish ♓','The Sun','Ruby',64,'Steady',NULL,60,'Steady',NULL,54,'Slow',NULL,59,'Steady',NULL,'2026-10-07 00:43:56','2026-10-07 01:00:40'),(294,'Pisces','Meen','Feb 19 – Mar 20','Month','2026-10-07','October brings a steady flow of planetary influences, beginning with the New Moon (Amavasya) on 10 Oct and culminating with the Full Moon (Purnima) on 26 Oct. A significant shift occurs on 18 Oct when the Sun moves from Virgo into your 8th house in Libra, altering your focus toward shared resources and inner transformation.\n\nCareer:\nThe Sun in your 7th house early in the month emphasizes partnerships and collaborative work environments. When the Sun transitions into your 8th house on 18 Oct, expect a period of deeper strategic planning behind the scenes rather than public spotlight.\n\nFinance:\nFinancial stability requires caution as Mercury and retrograde Venus occupy your 8th house, advising you against making speculative investments or risky loans. Keep your budget conservative and monitor shared expenses closely throughout the month.\n\nLove and Relationships:\nPartnerships face a period of introspection, especially after the Sun moves into the 8th house on 18 Oct, urging deeper emotional honesty between you and your partner. Use the Amavasya on 10 Oct to reset personal boundaries and clear any lingering misunderstandings.\n\nHealth:\nWith Ketu and the Moon frequently interacting with the 6th house early on, prioritize your well-being through proper rest and mindful eating habits. The Purnima on 26 Oct will help restore your emotional equilibrium.\n\nRemedy:\nFeed bananas or yellow lentils to stray cows on Thursdays to honor your sign lord Jupiter and invite positive energy.','#DAA520','9','11:45 AM - 12:32 PM','🌙 Transformative','Jupiter','Fish ♓','The Sun','Ruby